diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index a0d694362..bbe656870 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ For the new content or modified one in this mod (AdvCiv-SAS), only English trans
 - disabled tile coloring for worker recommended tile to improve (in `CvGame::updateColoredPlots` in CvGameInterface.cpp). These would take needless computation, both in debug mode ([see for related info this autoplay info](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-autoplay-let-the-ai-play-for-you-super-fast-gameplay--testing-tool-anyways-etc-in-map-loaded-save-file-new-game-etc-view-anyways-etc)) and even not in debug mode in regular games, plus most importantly our AI workers now use another logic in `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild` so the plots recommended are not even the ones that our AI workers would find best. They may be inaccurate if not so good plots, or confusing because we mostly want to see city site recommendations if we have to see anything rather, and i couldn't know if a colored circled tile/plot was a recommended tile to improve for a worker or a recommended site to plant/settle/found a city here (which are quite often btw better than the one i would have settled myself, see [Settlers (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#settlers-ai) for details or related info anyways etc). Hopefully for the better disabled for worker plots for all these reasons, while keeping all previous coloring such as city sites recommendations and such anyways etc. Note: the recommended settle spots do not always match what AI would do if it were to play for the human player in autoplay, so while our choosing logic is much stronger, i am not sure the colored settle points displayed to the human player are always the ones the AI would deem the best as per our reworked/enhanced `AIFoundValue::evaluate` so take them with some caution i'd say if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc.
 - removed the strategy text in next production to choose for city popup and next tech to choose popup ("Sid's tips"), as well as in civic to switch to popup ("Would you like to start a revolution?"), as they are oftentimes outdated or/and tedious to maintain anyways etc.
 - add the "Cannot be traded" and the "Can be researched multiple times" information tooltips in the tech advisor as well anyways etc. See for details [README.md#untradeable-techs-btrade-display-information](/README.md#untradeable-techs-btrade-display-information) for details.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5162+) Enlarged the foreign Advisors screen and beautified its panels so that we cleanly see the info of all 12 players without needing to scroll. Refactored the code so that if the advisor's screen dimensions are changed in their respective python file, the rest of the display dynamically follows and some info don't get stuck at old position. Change in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) and [CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py). See for details and examples [README.md#other-advisors-rework](/README.md#other-advisors-rework).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5162+) Enlarged the foreign Advisors screen and beautified its panels so that we cleanly see the info of all 12 players without needing to scroll at least not as much but anyways etc. Refactored the code so that if the advisor's screen dimensions are changed in their respective python file, the rest of the display dynamically follows and some info don't get stuck at old position. Change in [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) and [CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py). See for details and examples [README.md#other-advisors-rework](/README.md#other-advisors-rework).
 
